WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.770
A firework bursts: red,
then green, then violet.

2
00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:09.150
Each of those colours is light,
and light travels as photons.

3
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:13.490
Of the visible colours, a photon of
red light carries the least energy,

4
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.090
and a photon of violet light the most.

5
00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:19.690
So each colour needs photons
of a different energy.

6
00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.230
Why do fireworks come
in different colours?

7
00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:24.650
In this mission, you'll link wavelength,

8
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:28.720
frequency and energy, and see
how an atom gives out light.

9
00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:33.370
You'll find out what the bright lines in
hydrogen's spectrum reveal about its electron,

10
00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.730
and how many electrons
each level can hold.

11
00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:40.440
Your mission: explain where a
firework's colours come from.
